Subject: Hide the widget frame and re-host its body script on our own origin

Applies to: scriptAtlassianPure1.js  ->  scriptAtlassian1.js
Atlassian source: the embed loader served as /assets/embed.js by
                  https://jsd-widget.atlassian.com

Two changes, both load-bearing:

1. `visibility: hidden` / `opacity: 0` on the #jsd-widget iframe.
   The site never shows Atlassian's own UI. The frame is driven headlessly by
   our React code (src/components/SupportLauncher, src/components/contact) and
   only ever acts as the thing that performs the submission. Removing this
   exposes Atlassian's unstyled launcher in the corner of every page.

2. The iframe body script is pinned to an absolute tdspora.ai URL instead of
   being derived relative to the loader's own origin.
   This is what makes the iframe same-origin with the page, which is the only
   reason `contentWindow.document` can be read at all. Everything the site does
   with the widget depends on it.
   Consequence: the page and these bundles MUST be served from the same origin.
   On any other origin every read throws a cross-origin SecurityError;
   src/lib/supportWidget.js converts that into null and the UI falls back to
   the support portal.

